A||||1||JohnnyK||Best way to clean a 4cyl?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-01-2000||02:59 PM||||Ok, this engine has tons of crap on it (about an inch in some places of oil and dirt, etc) and I was wondering if i could hose some of the parts down with a pressure washer? (On top of the tranny near the shift linkage, for example) and then oil it down... I am not going to aim at any sensor or electric connectors? Surely this is ok if I degrease it and oil it after?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-01-2000||04:55 PM||||The engine MUST be cold.<P>don't oil it after.  that draws dirt and can cause a fire.<P>yes, as long as you are very carefull you can pressure wash. avoid aimind square at the edge of gaskets and seals. <P>DON'T spray the fiberglass insulation. if you have to work close to the insulation hang a bag down over it. You might want to do that anyway to keep dirt from sprayin on it.<P>dig off the really thick stuff with dull slotted screw driver. It'll signifigantly reduce the mess after. spray it with GUNK Engine Bright and let it soak in.<P>take the plug wires off and bag the distrubutor. <P>bag the MAP sensor. or tape off the top of it tightly. the top of the OEM and some aftermarket ones have vent holes. getting cleaner in these can screw them up.<P>take the air cleaner off and bag the TBI in 2 layers. bag it, tape it, then bag it and tape it again. use strong bags.||||reg||1
